//! The Rust exe patches (`docs/notes/rust_patches.md`): the arena's block
//! `patches.code`, one crate in three layers.
//!
//! - `raw`: generated by engine_026g.py from `engine_026g.tsv` and
//!   `fields_026g.tsv`: every game function (called directly in its own
//!   convention, or through a cdecl thunk), kernel32's imports, the address
//!   of each field. Unsafe, no logic. Only `vostok` names it.
//! - [`vostok`]: the engine's safe, typed API over `raw` (handles, enums,
//!   newtypes; the only `unsafe` blocks, each with its invariant), the hook
//!   system (the generated entries and shims, `Context`, `Original`,
//!   `Flow`), and the runtime (the log, the panic handler, memcpy/memset).
//! - The patches, a module each ([`suicide_key`]): `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`,
//!   `vostok` alone. A patch's hooks are its `<patch>.toml`, from which
//!   link_026g.py generates the entries (`hook_entries_026g.asm`) and the
//!   shims (`hooks_026g.rs`, inside `vostok`).
//!
//! link_026g.py refuses an address or a hand-made binding outside `raw`, and
//! a patch module that names `raw` or allows `unsafe` (rust_patches.md).

#![cfg_attr(not(test), no_std)]
// memcpy/memset are weak so the arena keeps one when a C patch (gcc emits
// its own) is linked beside this crate (rust_patches.md, vostok::rt).
#![cfg_attr(not(test), feature(linkage))]

#[cfg(test)]
extern crate std;

mod raw {
    include!("../../../engine_026g.rs");
}

pub mod vostok;

pub mod blackout;
pub mod suicide_key;
